# Not a bootable-image defconfig: this only produces a cross-toolchain SDK
# (via BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_ENVIRONMENT_SETUP) and the target libraries LK8000
# needs on Kobo, for use with `make TARGET=KOBO KOBO_SDK=y` in the main
# LK8000 repo. For a full alternate bootable Kobo Linux system (kernel,
# rootfs, secure boot, wifi, ...) see the separate buildroot-kobo project.
# Cortex-A9 -- NOT Cortex-A53. This is the LOWEST common denominator across
# every Kobo model LK8000 actually supports/detects (see Model.cpp and
# kobo/kernel/install.readme's "officially tested" list): Touch/Mini/Glo
# are Cortex-A8 (i.MX507), Aura/Glo HD/Touch 2.0/Aura 2 are Cortex-A9
# (i.MX6SL/SLL), and Clara HD/Nia/Libra H2O/Libra 2/Clara 2E are Cortex-A7
# (i.MX7) -- a genuinely mixed fleet. Neither Cortex-A8 nor Cortex-A9 have
# hardware integer divide (sdiv/udiv); Cortex-A7 does, but code built for
# the no-idiv baseline still runs correctly there (forward-compatible,
# just not maximally optimized) -- so ONE defconfig targeting Cortex-A9
# safely covers this whole device range, exactly like the main Makefile's
# own single hardcoded `-mtune=cortex-a7 -march=armv7-a` KOBO flags
# already do. Per-model defconfigs are not needed unless/until LK8000
# grows support for a genuinely different SoC vendor -- e.g. the newer
# MediaTek-based Clara Colour/Clara B&W/Libra Colour/Elipsa 2E (the
# separate buildroot-kobo project's territory) or Allwinner-based
# Elipsa/Sage.
#
# Buildroot derives its packages' own -mcpu/-march flags from this choice
# independently of the external toolchain below (via its toolchain-wrapper,
# which must be rebuilt after changing this -- `make toolchain-external-
# bootlin-dirclean toolchain-external-bootlin`, not just the packages).
# Getting this wrong is silent at build time and fails at runtime: it SIGILLs
# on real hardware the first time code hits an idiv (confirmed on-device:
# libGeographicLib/libcurl/libfreetype/libpng/libjpeg/libz all contained
# sdiv/udiv when BR2_cortex_a53 was selected here by mistake, copied
# uncritically from the separate buildroot-kobo project's Kobo Clara
# Colour -- a different, Cortex-A53 device).
BR2_arm=y
BR2_cortex_a9=y
BR2_ARM_ENABLE_NEON=y
BR2_ARM_ENABLE_VFP=y
# Bootlin prebuilt toolchain (glibc, GCC >= 14) instead of Kobo's original
# vendor Linaro 4.9.4 toolchain -- the old one can't compile LK8000, which
# requires -std=c++20. LK8000 ships its own glibc/libstdc++/ld.so to the
# device (see the KOBO block in the main Makefile's LDFLAGS) rather than
# relying on the stock Kobo firmware's runtime, so a newer glibc here is
# fine: only the app's own bundled runtime needs to match this toolchain,
# not the device's stock userspace.
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_BOOTLIN=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_BOOTLIN_ARMV7_EABIHF_GLIBC_BLEEDING_EDGE=y
BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_ENVIRONMENT_SETUP=y
# LK8000 dependencies (see LK8000/Scripts/kobo-build-rootfs for the
# equivalent shell-script-based build of these same libraries)
BR2_PACKAGE_BOOST=y
BR2_PACKAGE_FREETYPE=y
BR2_PACKAGE_GEOGRAPHICLIB=y
BR2_PACKAGE_JPEG=y
BR2_PACKAGE_JPEG_TURBO=y
BR2_PACKAGE_LIBCURL=y
BR2_PACKAGE_OPENSSL=y
BR2_PACKAGE_LIBCURL_OPENSSL=y
BR2_PACKAGE_LIBPNG=y
BR2_PACKAGE_ZZIPLIB=y
